{"path":"program/raise","title":"raise","titleHtml":"raise","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/c/program/raise","section":"program","kind":"page","summary":"Sends signal sig to the program. The signal handler, specified using signal(), is invoked.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/c/program\"><code>&lt;signal.h&gt;</code></a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\"><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> raise<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">int</span> sig <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Sends signal sig to the program. The signal handler, specified using <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\">signal()</a></span>, is invoked.\n</p><p>If the user-defined signal handling strategy is not set using <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\">signal()</a></span> yet, it is implementation-defined whether the signal will be ignored or default handler will be invoked. \n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td>  sig\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td>  the signal to be sent. It can be an implementation-defined value or one of the following values:\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/program/SIG_types\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>SIGABRT</span><span>SIGFPE</span><span>SIGILL</span><span>SIGINT</span><span>SIGSEGV</span><span>SIGTERM</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   defines signal types <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(macro constant)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi c source-c\">​<span class=\"nu0\">0</span>​</span></code> upon success, non-zero value on failure.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"c\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;signal.h&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">void</span> signal_handler<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span> <a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\"><span class=\"kw497\">signal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Received signal&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\"><span class=\"kw497\">signal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw4\">void</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"co1\">// Install a signal handler.</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\"><span class=\"kw497\">signal</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/program/SIG_types\"><span class=\"kw507\">SIGTERM</span></a>, signal_handler<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Sending signal&nbsp;%d<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, <a href=\"/w/c/program/SIG_types\"><span class=\"kw507\">SIGTERM</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    raise<span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/c/program/SIG_types\"><span class=\"kw507\">SIGTERM</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/c/io/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw850\">printf</span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"Exit main()<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Sending signal 15\nReceived signal 15\nExit main()</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"References\">References</h3>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-17\">\n<ul><li> C17 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2018): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.14.2.1 The raise function (p: 194-195)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-11\">\n<ul><li> C11 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:2011): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.14.2.1 The raise function (p: 267)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c99\">\n<ul><li> C99 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1999): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 7.14.2.1 The raise function (p: 248)\n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<div class=\"t-ref-std-c89\">\n<ul><li> C89/C90 standard (ISO/IEC 9899:1990): \n</li></ul>\n<dl><dd><ul><li> 4.7.2.1 The raise function \n</li></ul>\n</dd></dl>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/c/program/signal\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>signal</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>   sets a signal handler for particular signal  <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/program/raise\">C++ documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>raise</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"References","id":"References"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C reference"},{"path":"program","title":"Program support utilities"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"raise","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Sends signal sig to the program. The signal handler, specified using signal(), is invoked."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"sig","children":[{"label":"SIGABRT, SIGFPE, SIGILL, …","note":"defines signal types"}]},{"label":"Return value","note":"0 upon success, non-zero value on failure."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"signal","note":"sets a signal handler for particular signal"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":180,"codeBlockCount":2}
